<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colwyn Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Colwyn Bay is a seaside town on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, in Conwy county, within the area of the early medieval kingdom of Rhos. It grew rapidly as a resort after the arrival of the railway in the mid-19th century. Nearby lie Rhos-on-Sea and the hill of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryn-euryn">Bryn Euryn</a>, possibly a royal seat of Rhos, and the Welsh Mountain Zoo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/colwyn-bay.jpg" alt="Colwyn Bay" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steve Daniels · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Station_Road_in_Colwyn_Bay_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2090426.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
